nncp (8.13.0+git20260925132658.f28c62f-1rhizomatica1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sp: per-node pinginterval (seconds). An HF neighbour can send the SP
    keepalive rarely, since each one costs a modem turn; others keep the
    default. The HERMES mesh sets 600 s. pinginterval: 0 is rejected.
  * hfmodem: never open the TNC next to a daemon that holds it. When the
    hfmodem proxy daemon is running and its dial fails, nncp-call now
    reports the daemon's error instead of opening a second control
    connection to Mercury, which serves one client and lost the TNC to
    it. Direct TNC dialling remains when no daemon is running.

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@rhizomatica.org>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0100

nncp (8.13.0+git20260923205140.04147c2-1rhizomatica1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sp: keep a session alive while a packet is still arriving. A session
    was dropped when no whole SP packet had arrived for 2 min; on HF one
    file packet takes minutes, so calls ended at 2:00 after the handshake
    with no file delivered. Liveness now also follows the bytes; a silent
    peer is still dropped at 2 min.

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@rhizomatica.org>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0100

nncp (8.13.0+git20260923.7290b51-1rhizomatica1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuilt on upstream develop (git.stargrave.org, module
    go.stargrave.org/nncp/v8), which now carries the HF modem transport
    and per-node nopad. Fork-only changes on top:
  * NNCPPv4 plain packets with a variable-length path (~240 B less per
    packet), opt-in per node and per area (pktv4); everything else still
    gets NNCPPv3, byte-identical to 8.13.0.
  * hfmodem: an answered session ends when the TNC reports DISCONNECTED,
    instead of idling to its online deadline; nothing is written to the
    TNC between sessions (stray bytes stalled Mercury's broadcasts).
  * postinst no longer resets the spool to 755 root: it only creates it.

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@rhizomatica.org>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

nncp (8.13.0-6rhizomatica1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make nopad a per-node config option (nopad: true in nncp.hjson)
    instead of auto-detecting from HF connection type. Both initiator
    and responder now honor the config. Also adds cfgdir save/load support.

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@rhizomatica.org>  Wed, 19 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
